  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since \\(y=2x\\), the second relation gives \\(z=2y=2(2x)=4x\\). Substituting both expressions makes all three terms multiples of \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx+y+z=x+2x+4x=(1+2+4)x=\\boxed{7x}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
